Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Singular field of a scalar point particle\
\>", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.537001967604075*^9, 3.5370019864838*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We give a fourth order approximation to the singular field of a point \
scalar charge in various spacetimes. In all cases, this depends on the \
position and four velocity of the particle and on the position where the \
field is evaluated. We use the following definitions:\n\nr1 - particle\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s radial position\n\[Theta]1 - particle\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
polar coordinate (assumed to be \[Pi]/2)\n\[Phi]1 - \
particle\[CloseCurlyQuote]s azimuthal coordinate\n\nr - radial position where \
the field is evaluated\n\[Theta] - polar position where the field is \
evaluated\n\[Phi] - azimuthal position where the field is evaluated\n\n\
\[CapitalDelta]r = r - r1\n\[CapitalDelta]\[Theta] = \[Theta] - \[Theta]1 = \
\[Theta]-\[Pi]/2\n\[CapitalDelta]\[Phi] = \[Phi] - \[Phi]1\n\[CapitalDelta]Q \
= sin(\[CapitalDelta]\[Phi]/2)\n\[CapitalDelta]R = sin(\[CapitalDelta]\[Phi])\
\n\nur1, ut1, u\[Phi]1 - components of the particle\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
four-velocity (assume u\[Theta]1=0)\n\ne1 = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["u", "t"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm"],
 " - \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]energy\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] constant of motion\
\nl1 = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["u", "\[Phi]"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm"],
 " - \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]angular momentum\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] constant \
of motion\n\nM - mass of the central black hole\na - spin of the central \
black hole (in units of M)\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.537002031344637*^9, 3.5370020620271397`*^9}, {
  3.537002110079599*^9, 3.537002110280136*^9}, {3.537002309901874*^9, 
  3.5370023720172873`*^9}, {3.53700242383818*^9, 3.5370025373132153`*^9}, {
  3.537002657487788*^9, 3.537002847895771*^9}, {3.53700287861339*^9, 
  3.537002928091692*^9}, {3.537002970732856*^9, 3.537003010692143*^9}, {
  3.537003795042273*^9, 3.53700380542964*^9}, {3.537017466358819*^9, 
  3.5370174684226723`*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Schwarzschild", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.537002014176443*^9, 3.537002017726886*^9}}],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Generic (equatorial) geodesic", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.537002123633374*^9, 3.537002131794105*^9}}],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note that the four-velocity of a general equatorial geodesic in \
Schwarzschild may be given in terms of the constants of motion:\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[{
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["ur1", "2"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["e1", "2"], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "M"}], "-", "r1"}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["l1", "2"], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["r1", "2"]}], ")"}]}], 
     SuperscriptBox["r1", "3"]]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"ut1", "=", 
   RowBox[{"e1", " ", 
    FractionBox["r1", 
     RowBox[{"r1", "-", 
      RowBox[{"2", "M"}]}]]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"u\[Phi]1", "=", 
   FractionBox["l1", 
    SuperscriptBox["r1", "2"]]}]}],
  CellChangeTimes->{{3.529244673438335*^9, 3.529244675026743*^9}, {
    3.530978977838888*^9, 3.5309789912369843`*^9}, {3.5353784360986023`*^9, 
    3.535378444291664*^9}, {3.5365620994214287`*^9, 3.536562102604096*^9}, {
    3.536562218022279*^9, 3.536562270608309*^9}, 3.5365626288543587`*^9, {
    3.536563835984952*^9, 3.536563864808775*^9}, {3.537003290438818*^9, 
    3.5370033112154408`*^9}}],
 "\n\nWe have used this fact to simplify the following expression for the \
singular field"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.537003615938632*^9, 3.537003777196761*^9}, 
   3.537004483714533*^9, {3.53700561082703*^9, 3.537005726815544*^9}}],

